Google C++ Testing Framework
============================

This tree vendors Google Test for REX's Linux-only test runs.
For upstream documentation, see http://code.google.com/p/googletest/.

Requirements
------------

These are the base requirements to build Google Test from a source package:

  * GNU-compatible Make
  * POSIX-standard shell
  * POSIX regular expressions (regex.h)
  * A C++ compiler supported by REX

Build Notes
-----------

The REX build integrates gtest as part of the test support. If you need a
standalone build, compile `src/gtest-all.cc` with `${GTEST_DIR}/include` and
`${GTEST_DIR}` on the include path. For example:

  g++ -isystem ${GTEST_DIR}/include -I${GTEST_DIR} \
      -pthread -c ${GTEST_DIR}/src/gtest-all.cc
  ar -rv libgtest.a gtest-all.o
